{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner decision on aaf573dd, as corrected by cd6678d2. I accept your recommendation. 6d96e044 holds for a room's scopes, with these changes. Stopping there was the right call.\n\n**Route 1: repair it.** Refuse a `found` or `first-key` whose founder key equals the recovery key. Join and enrol already keep the two keys apart, and creation should do the same. The read is the smaller part of this: a stolen key in that shape keeps the recovery key's authority. File this under its own request. If it needs a new Membership or Directory definition, name the pin in the review request, because the deployment that creates rooms on it needs that named. Do not repair existing rooms. The docs state that a room with this shape ends it only by rotating the recovery key.\n\n**Route 2: state it, no repair.** The register is its own authority, and a room's revocation does not reach it. The route reads nothing of the room. Under policy open, any key can sign `found`, so the read grants no one more than they could already get. `docs/security/` states that an operator responding to a stolen key must also remove it from the register's founders list.\n\n**The bound: 1200 s plus clock difference, not 900 s.** State it that way, with its parts: up to 300 s for a scope's observation of membership, then the 900 s window. State that nobody has measured a real clock difference. Everywhere 6d96e044 or the docs say \"the rest of the window\", use this bound. State also that a revoked key's acts can still be accepted during those 300 s, since that matters more than the read.\n\n**What a revoked key reads.** List what you found: the summary with all live items, including other members' lanes, `query-items`, entry 0, its own entries, filtered history and log, its own lane's summary and that lane's retained definition. Name what it cannot read too.\n\nThe cases you did not run stay named as not run: `install`, `found` under policy open, hosted and application scopes, and real clock differences.\n\nNext: file the signed-read head with the docs under 09083039, and the refusal under the new request. Both come after the dap mcp writer repair in your own order.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}